
# Structured Gujarati Legal Judgement Replication System

## Project Goal
- Build a Structured Gujarati Legal Judgement Replication System
- Replicate:
  - exact format
  - structure
  - section order
  - legal drafting style
  - court layout
- Goal is NOT:
  - chatbot
  - QA system
  - normal RAG summarization
- Goal IS:
  - production-oriented legal document replication pipeline

---

# Current Problem

## Existing Workflow
OCR → Chunking → Embedding → RAG → LLM Generation

## Problems with Current Approach
- Generates summary-style outputs
- Loses legal formatting
- Breaks numbering hierarchy
- Structure becomes inconsistent
- Hallucinates legal flow
- Does not preserve court document style

---

# Correct System Architecture

## Target Workflow

Judgement PDF
↓
GLM-OCR Extraction
↓
Layout + Section Parsing
↓
Structured JSON Template
↓
Section-wise Retrieval
↓
Structure-Constrained Generation
↓
Final Gujarati Legal Judgement Replication

---

# Core Architectural Shift

## Wrong Approach
- Generic OCR extraction
- Random chunking
- Semantic-only retrieval
- Free-form generation

## Correct Approach
- Layout-aware OCR
- Section parsing
- Structured extraction
- Template schema generation
- Section-wise retrieval
- Template-constrained generation
- Final layout reconstruction

---

# What Must Be Preserved

## Court Formatting
- Official court layout
- Header structure
- Legal formatting
- Alignment
- Spacing
- Page structure

## Legal Tone
- Gujarati legal terminology
- Court drafting style
- Official legal language

## Numbering Hierarchy
Examples:
- (1)
- (1.1)
- (1.2)
- (2)
- (2.1)

Must preserve:
- hierarchy
- order
- indentation
- subsection relationships

## Party Structure
- Applicant formatting
- Respondent formatting
- Advocate details
- Address blocks

## Judgement Structure
- Facts
- Arguments
- Observations
- Findings
- Orders
- References

---

# Required System Components

## 1. OCR Layer

### Recommended Tools
- GLM-OCR
- PaddleOCR (fallback)

### OCR Goals
- Accurate Gujarati extraction
- Preserve line order
- Preserve coordinates
- Preserve layout information

---

## 2. Layout Understanding Layer

### Required Features
- Header detection
- Section boundary detection
- Paragraph grouping
- Numbering extraction
- Layout segmentation
- Table/block identification

### Recommended Tools
- LayoutParser
- Docling
- pdfplumber
- pymupdf
- Detectron2 layout models

---

## 3. Structured Parser

### Purpose
Convert OCR text into structured legal schema.

### Example JSON Structure

{
  "header": {},
  "case_info": {},
  "parties": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "title": "",
      "content": "",
      "subsections": []
    }
  ],
  "order": {}
}

---

# Retrieval System

## Important Rule
Do NOT use:
- random chunk retrieval
- semantic-only retrieval

## Correct Retrieval
Retrieve by:
- section type
- legal role
- numbering structure
- template similarity

### Example
Retrieve:
- “ORDER section examples”
Instead of:
- “nearest semantic chunks”

---

# Generation System

## Wrong Generation
Generate entire judgement freely.

## Correct Generation
Generate:
- section-by-section
- structure-constrained
- template-guided
- formatting-aware

### Example
Generate subsection 2.3 using:
- matching legal template
- numbering structure
- section schema

---

# Recommended Pipeline

## Phase 1 — OCR
PDF → OCR text + coordinates

## Phase 2 — Layout Understanding
Detect:
- headers
- sections
- numbering
- blocks
- paragraphs

## Phase 3 — Structured JSON
Convert judgement into structured schema.

## Phase 4 — Template Learning
Learn:
- section order
- formatting patterns
- drafting style
- numbering structure

## Phase 5 — Section-wise Retrieval
Retrieve:
- similar section templates
- similar legal structures

## Phase 6 — Controlled Generation
Generate:
- section-by-section
- under strict structure constraints

## Phase 7 — Final Reconstruction
Rebuild:
- final court-style judgement document

---

